  "title": "Tigranes the Great",
  "summary": "Tigranes II ruled Armenia from 95 BCE, set on the throne by the Parthian king Mithradates II, until his death in 55 BCE. He founded a new, more central capital, Tigranocerta, for his enlarged kingdom. Roman wars under Lucullus and then Pompey followed, and he ended as a Roman client.",
